# Prerequisites
*.d

# Object files
*.o
*.ko
*.obj
*.elf

# Linker output
*.ilk
*.map
*.exp

# Precompiled Headers
*.gch
*.pch

# Libraries
# NB: *.a is deliberately NOT ignored here - ACME uses .a for 6502 source files
# (see its docs: "Please use '.a' as the file name extension of ACME source
# code files"), so ignoring it would silently drop assembly sources.
*.lib
*.la
*.lo

# Shared objects (inc. Windows DLLs)
*.dll
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib

# Executables
*.exe
*.out
*.app
*.i*86
*.x86_64
*.hex

# Debug files
*.dSYM/
*.su
*.idb
*.pdb

# Kernel Module Compile Results
*.mod*
*.cmd
.tmp_versions/
modules.order
Module.symvers
Mkfile.old
dkms.conf

# debug information files
*.dwo

# Claude Code state staged for the first devcontainer rebuild (contains credentials)
.devcontainer/.claude-seed/

# Claude Code: track this project's own instructions, its remaining local
# skills, and its shared project settings, ignore the installed toolkit
# (agents, commands, hooks, gsd-core) and per-machine settings.local.json.
#
# CLAUDE.md is tracked as of 2026-08-01. It was never per-machine -- it carries
# the project's own standing rules, including the hard rule that
# mcp__plugin_c64-re-tools_vice__* is the only route to the emulator. Being
# caught by the blanket `.claude/*` meant those rules lived in one working copy
# and a fresh clone silently got none of them, which is the wrong failure
# direction for a rule whose whole job is to stop something being rebuilt.
#
# settings.json is tracked as of this migration: it declares the c64-re-tools
# plugin marketplace (extraKnownMarketplaces) and enables the plugin
# (enabledPlugins), which every session needs, so it must be shared -- not
# per-machine. Machine-local overrides still go in settings.local.json, which
# stays ignored by the blanket `.claude/*` below. (The former `!.claude/mcp/`
# negation is gone with the MCP source, now in the c64-re-tools plugin repo.)
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/

# scratch notes
anything.*

# transient VICE probe screenshots (evidence is re-captured by tools/recover.mjs)
recovery/*/dumps/probe-*.png

# host-side VICE supervisor output (tools/vice-supervisor.sh): crash logs and
# the restart epoch file, regenerated fresh on every supervisor start -- not
# a project artifact, just evidence for the current debugging session.
# The .bak-* form is the same state moved aside during a clean-slate restart
# (see 01.2-CRITERION-13-EVIDENCE.md § 1) -- kept on disk for its crash logs,
# still not a project artifact.
.vice-supervisor/
.vice-supervisor.bak-*/

# Deployed copies of the vice MCP server's resources. The MCP implementation
# now lives in the c64-re-tools plugin (henols/c64-re-tools), not this repo,
# but at runtime it still deploys these host-bound artifacts into THIS
# project's tools/ (it resolves the project root via CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR), so
# the ignore lines stay here. They are regenerated on the plugin server's
# first tool call and are disposable: never hand-edit them.
/tools/vice-broker.mjs
/tools/vice-launcher.sh
/tools/container-guard.mjs
/tools/broker-state.mjs
/tools/broker-launch.mjs
/tools/broker-kill.mjs
/tools/broker-epoch.mjs
/tools/broker-control.mjs
# The deploy manifest (Phase 01.6 plan 03) -- install-resources.mjs's own
# record of what it has placed under tools/, and the ONLY input its prune
# step ever consults (never a directory walk -- tools/ is mixed, and also
# holds tracked reverse-engineering tooling). Disposable like every other
# entry in this block: a real host regenerates it on the next deploy.
/tools/.vice-deployed.json

# The vice MCP server's node_modules moved out with it to the c64-re-tools
# plugin (provisioned into the plugin's own install dir by its SessionStart
# hook, never here). This unanchored entry stays as a backstop so any stray
# node_modules/ at any depth never pollutes `git status`.
node_modules/
